# THESE RULES DO NOT REACH THE LIVE RESPONSE. Measured 08.09.2026, months
# after they shipped: /wp-content/uploads/ and /fonts/ come back with no
# Cache-Control at all. The host's own hashed output under /assets/ IS cached,
# but that is its default for build output, not this file being honoured.
# The rules that actually take effect live in src/lib/asset-headers.ts, applied
# from src/server.ts. Kept only so the intent is documented if the site ever
# moves to a host that reads _headers.
#
# Versioned WordPress migration assets never change in place. Cache them at
# the browser and edge for one year; new uploads use a new path or filename.
/wp-content/uploads/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Other copied WordPress assets are likewise content-addressed or versioned.
/wp-content/plugins/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/wp-includes/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
